<h2 class="wp-block-heading">In the Community</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/devonthink-ai-assisted-naming-and-filing">DEVONthink AI-Assisted Naming and Filing</a> · Labs Discussion Board</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A member reported naming and filing roughly 800 documents for $2.45 after following the Labs walkthrough. The workflow reads the document for its date and meaning, then uses those details to name and file it consistently.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/local-models-and-document-review">Local Models and Document Review</a> · Labs Discussion Board</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A member shared a detailed comparison of local models, Apple’s private cloud models, and Claude on document-review tasks. In these tests, finding relevant information wasn’t the biggest obstacle: confidently adding false claims was. A useful account of where their experiments succeeded and fell short.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://macsparky.circle.so/c/labs-discussion-board/digital-recorder-recommendation">Digital Recorder Recommendation</a> · Labs Discussion Board</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">An interesting hardware puzzle: a recorder that can be operated in the dark, with its screens and lights covered. The discussion gets into why a physical switch and feedback you can feel matter when you can’t look at the device.</p>



